        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF152 adds support for importing text modules in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2024854" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2024854</a> (this uses the <code class="notranslate">with</code> clause <code class="notranslate">{type: "text"}</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto">This adds the text type subfeature, and corresponding <code class="notranslate">text</code> destination for fetch requests. This doesn't seem to be supported in Chrome or Safari (quick search). I've set other platforms to false, except for BUN</p>
